  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001099",
        "SRC-001107"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SJ Build: SP18-059, 100% affordable, up to 365 units.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001799"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City of San Jose permit SP18-059 (Special Use Permit, folder year 2018), status Approved, issue date 2020-02-11: \"Special Use Permit to allow the demolition of two industrial buildings, removal of three (3) ordinance-sized trees, for the construction a 100% affordable housing (excluding the manager�s units) project with up to 365 multi-family residential units with\" (city text cut off at 255 characters)",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001956"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The site has two towers: McEvoy Apartments (workforce, 224 units) and Dupont Apartments (family, 141 one- to three-bedroom units). CTCAC CA-21-746 (Dec. 2021) covers the McEvoy tower only: 140 studios and 84 one-bedrooms, 222 restricted units (112 at 30% AMI, 20 at 50%, 90 at 60%), 20 VASH project-based vouchers, total project cost $132,176,093. SERA shows the McEvoy tower as 142 studios and 82 one-bedrooms.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002315",
        "SRC-002312"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SF YIMBY (Dec. 2021): about $135 million total cost including $66.4 million construction and $40 million soft costs; Google Endeavor LLC provided funding in November 2020; workforce tower construction expected to start mid-2022.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002314"
      ]
    }
  ],
